## The code

- F32: `dashboard/scripts/storytime/check-storytime-pictures.ts`. Each row class of each requested week is selected on its own. The book rows of week N are requested when the manifest holds a job for a book row of week N, or when it holds no job for any row of week N. The card rows of week N follow the same rule with the card rows. Every requested row with no job fails. A class of a week that the batch does not request prints one skip line before the summary line: `skip  book rows of week N: the batch holds no job for them`. The summary counts the requested rows only. The exit codes stay. The usage text and the code comment state this rule.
- F35: `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/pictures.ts`. `storytimeCardPictureRows` keeps a set of the words and a map of the row ids. Two words of one week that share a slug throw, and the message keeps the prefix `card picture word repeat:` and names both words. The round 4 word check stays.
